<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Turkic Khaganate</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Second Khaganate</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Turkic Khaganate was the revived <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-khaganate">Göktürk</a> state established in the late seventh century, after a period of subjection to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a>. It is known for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkhon-inscriptions">Orkhon inscriptions</a>, the earliest substantial texts in a Turkic language. The Gokturk Empire profile discusses its military and governance, and it was overthrown in the mid-eighth century by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghurs</a> and their allies.</p></div>
